# The intake ledger's DATA — never the tool, which is bin/intake and is tracked.
# These lines came out on 2026-08-30 on the stated ground that the repository had
# been made private. It had not: checked anonymously against the GitHub API the
# same day, `private: false`, `visibility: public`. Restored by operator decision.
#
# Know what this does and does not do. `.gitignore` governs `git add`, so it
# guards the CLI and the local app — the paths a session and the Sync button use.
# It has NO effect on GitHub's contents API, which is how the portal writes from
# a browser; that path is guarded in the portal, which reads this repository's
# visibility and refuses to sync while it is public. Both guards are needed and
# neither substitutes for the other.
#
# To reverse: make the repository private FIRST, verify it, then delete these
# lines. In that order — the history cannot be un-published afterwards.
intake/events.jsonl
intake/units.json
raw/health/intake/
